# Line endings: normalize ALL text files to LF, in the repo and the working tree, on every
# platform. Git auto-detects binary and leaves it untouched (binaries are also pinned below).
#
# Why repo-wide: with core.autocrlf=true, Windows checkout smudges LF blobs to CRLF, and
# Vite/vitest's transform mis-parses a regex-in-a-template-literal under CRLF -- which silently
# broke scripts/generate-sitemap.test.mjs (#496). Forcing LF everywhere closes that trap for
# every source type, not just the one file that happened to trigger it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Critical shell scripts stay LF even if content sniffing ever wavers (husky, git hooks).
.husky/_/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never apply text/eol/diff conversion (explicit guard over text=auto).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Card data and generated files: collapsed in GitHub diffs and left out of language stats.
# They stay in git (admin and the scripts write them), and keep their text diff locally.
# Listed by name: playstyleGuides.json beside them is prose people read, so it stays reviewed.
apps/web/public/data/allCards.json linguist-generated
apps/web/public/data/previewCards.json linguist-generated
apps/web/public/data/collection/*.json linguist-generated
scripts/data/promo-printings.json linguist-generated
middleware-data/card-slugs.json linguist-generated
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated
